**The change fits in `cli.js` alone.**

One call to make first. `buildRows()` gives six fields. `toTable` drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose. I would print all six in JSON. Same rows, no lossy trim.

```js
// src/cli.js
const USAGE = 'usage: cli.js report [--json]';

function main(argv) {
  const [command, ...flags] = argv;
  if (command !== 'report' || flags.some((f) => f !== '--json')) {
    process.stderr.write(USAGE + '\n');
    return 1;
  }
  const rows = buildRows();
  const out = flags.includes('--json')
    ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2)
    : toTable(rows);
  process.stdout.write(out + '\n');
  return 0;
}
```

`report.js` and `format.js` stay untouched.

